// D1 round 10 / SP0 — a recorded aggregate COMPOSED INTO another aggregate.
// `note_alias`'s U2 gate asked whether the STORED VALUE is a `&mut`, so the
// struct-typed store `h.i = inn` was rejected and the edge `h -> inn` never
// existed. `inn.r -> v` WAS recorded, but the deposit lands on root `h` and
// each_root(h) = {h}, so the summary was lost WHOLE (LOGOS_DUMP_FLOWS printed
// no line at all for the callee, against the depth-1 twin's `out1<-0x1`).
// The gate now also admits an aggregate that transitively holds a `&mut` —
// which is a write path, i.e. exactly what an alias edge is consumed for.
//
// ⚠ RE-AUTHORED, D1 round 11. The line this fixture exists to test used to be
// REDUNDANT: `h` was built as `Mid { i: Inner { r: v } }`, i.e. already aliased
// to `v` through the LITERAL, so `h.i = inn` could be deleted and the
// diagnostic survived — the fixture stayed rc=1 under a control revert of the
// rule it names, which makes it a NON-WITNESS for that rule. MEASURED, one
// rule at a time, with a green checkpoint on both sides: the control drops
// `bc_holds_mut_ref_type` from the U2 store door in borrow_flow_summary.inc
// (one occurrence, asserted), rebuilds logosc, and restores md5-identically.
// OLD file under that control: rc=1, unmoved. THIS file under it: rc=0, the
// diagnostic gone — 3 reds in the 159-test witness set (this file, sp1, and
// the X3 mask gate, whose bc_flow_mask/x3_sp0_reauth.logos is this shape), and
// 159/159 with the arm restored. `h` is now built over a
// DIFFERENT vec (`w`), so the aggregate STORE is the only alias path from
// `h.i.r` to `v`; and `ws` is dead at the `c.bump()` line (its last use is the
// call), so only `vs`'s loan can produce the diagnostic. Its MASK is asserted
// separately, by bc_flow_mask_gate.sh over bc_flow_mask/x3_sp0_reauth.logos.
package bc_d1r10_sp0_aggregate_composed_in;
use logos.mem.collections.vec;
#[borrow_carrying]
struct B { p: &i64 }
struct C { v: i64 }
impl C {
    fn mk(&self) -> B { return B { p: &self.v }; }
    fn bump(&mut self) { self.v = self.v + 1i64; }
}
struct Inner { r: &mut Vec<B> }
struct Mid { i: Inner }
fn stash2(c: &C, v: &mut Vec<B>, w: &mut Vec<B>) {
    let inn: Inner = Inner { r: v };
    let mut h: Mid = Mid { i: Inner { r: w } };
    h.i = inn;
    h.i.r.push(c.mk());
}
fn main() -> i64 {
    let mut c: C = C { v: 1i64 };
    let mut vs: Vec<B> = Vec::new();
    let mut ws: Vec<B> = Vec::new();
    stash2(&c, &mut vs, &mut ws);
    c.bump();                        // must be REFUSED
    return *vs.get(0u64).p;
}
